          "statement": "ed-end libraries, the extracted DNA was fragmented to an average size of \napproximately 400 bp using the NEXTFLEX Rapid DNA-Seq kit. Sequencing was conducted on an \nIllumina NovaSeq (Illumina, San Diego, USA) following the manufacturer's instructions. Adaptors \nwere trimmed from Illumina reads and low-quality reads (length < 50 bp, quality value < 20, or having \nN bases) were removed using Fastp (version 0.20.0). The annotation was conducted using Diamond \n(version 0.8.35) against the KEGG database (http://www.genome.jp/keeg/) with an e-value cutoff of \n1e-5. The raw sequencing data in this study has been submitted to National Center for Biotechnology \nInformation (NCBI) with project number PRJNA1128434. \n"
        }
